 - Cumulative read coverages for each indexed BAM file are plotted by counting and sorting all reads overlapping a “window” of specified length (plotFingerprint).\r
 - Production of coverage track files (bigWig), with the coverage calculated as the number of reads per consecutive windows of predefined size (bamCoverage), and normalized through various available methods (e.g., Reads Per Kilobase per Million mapped reads; RPKM). The coverage track files are used to calculate scores per selected genomic regions (computeMatrix), typically genes, and a heatmap, based on the scores associated with these genomic regions, is produced (plotHeatmap).\r
